  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Negative input to positive RAW / reference / trigger",
      "notes": [
        "Input low-voltage shaped negative pulses only; RAW is positive around nominal0.623V.",
        "BASE_ADC is reference only. Amplitude=PEAK_ADC minus event-before RAW baseline.",
        "Output and input protection/current limits need bench validation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Positive precision peak capture / freeze / reset",
      "notes": [
        "HOLD high freezes capture by selecting BASE. PEAK_RESET high resets storage to BASE.",
        "HOLD_CAP is high impedance: keep capacitor/diode/buffer close; no external test pad.",
        "Analog prototype; hold droop/settling/pileup, nonlinear response and acquisition timing require measurement."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "USB, AT32 module and physical interfaces",
      "notes": [
        "Carrier60x32mm. Module body x8..34,y6..26; all its components face UP.",
        "SMA five-pin vertical pattern uses center signal plus four grounds on5.08mm square. Validate low-cost part drawing before purchase.",
        "G-S-G wire pads are an alternative signal connection. Do not connect two active sources.",
        "All3.3V comes from module M1 pin6; no independent carrier3.3V supply.",
        "USB data flow J1 -> D90 -> M1. IO1 and IO2 pairs of D90 internally connected."
      ]
    }
  ],
